{
  "_doc": "Desired state of the NVIDIA Shield TV Pro units, compared READ-ONLY by shield-check.py (applying stays manual: a past automatic debloat pass broke Play Store and voice search). disabled_packages: must be disabled if installed; not installed at all is fine. required_enabled_packages: must be installed and not disabled. absent_packages: must not be installed. settings: the exact string 'settings get <namespace> <key>' prints; an unset key reads back as the literal null (system nv_power_mode 0 is the Max performance processor mode). component_lists: a colon-separated list of Android component names; every listed component must be present, and the short form pkg/.Cls equals pkg/pkg.Cls. Device-specific settings are deliberately NOT listed, so the check never flags them: HDMI-CEC, IR remote, volume-control mode, Wi-Fi versus Ethernet, audio output, display mode and the device name (the bedroom unit has CEC and IR off on purpose).",
